On Sat, 2008-02-23 at 02:20 +0100, Thomas Jarosch wrote:
> first of all thank you for mlmmj

You are very welcome.

> I was searching for a replacement for my (dead?) ecartis installation
> and that's when I found mlmmj.

... and their last news post is titled "Patching more buffer overflows."

> Attached is a patch that let's you disable the automatic bounce =20
> handling and for example set the bounce address to =20
> postmaster@domain.com. I needed this because the subscriptions etc. =20
> are automatically generated by another system and I need to =20
> fix/unsubscribe the people there.

Your patch is very clean, but (when configured to) it changes the bounce
address from

listname+bounces-1464-morten=AFdelingp.dk@example.com

to

something@example.com

I think it would be better to keep the bounce information, and have the
bounce mail go to

something+1464-morten=AFdelingp.dk@example.com

That way you can both control where bounces are sent, and see who is
bouncing. Could I convince you to make the patch so?

> If all goes well mlmmj will be pushed out to 1.500+ servers
> as transparent replacement for ecartis at the end of April :-)

I think it's safe to say that you will have the largest mlmmj
installation on the internet :-)

Morten

